.TH AVR\-FIREWALL\-FLOW\-SUMMARIES 1 "" "avr 0.1.5" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-firewall-flow-summaries \- Show per-VM network activity summaries captured at VM stop.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr firewall flow-summaries
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show per-VM network activity summaries captured at VM stop.
.PP
Each row is the totals + top-N destinations + per-rule drop counters for one VM run. Use ``--with-drops`` to triage what the firewall blocked after editing a rule, ``--vm`` to look up a specific run from a job log.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified.
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository ID. (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-vm\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter to a single VM ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-with\-drops\fR
Show only summaries where the firewall blocked at least one flow.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Max summaries to return. (default: 20)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit raw JSON instead of a table.
.SH SEE ALSO
